<figure id="S3.F8.sf5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2604.03044v1/acc_vs_token_sep_bar_SWEBench.png" id="S3.F8.sf5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/397;" width="476" height="397" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(e) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F8.sf6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2604.03044v1/acc_vs_token_sep_bar_pinch.png" id="S3.F8.sf6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/397;" width="476" height="397" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(f) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Comparison of model performance (left bars) and token consumption (right bars) across six benchmarks. Qwen3.5-35B-A3B and JoyAI-LLM Flash are instruct models, “GLM-4.7-Flash-T” refers to GLM-4.7-Flash-Thinking, which is included due to its comparable performance.</figcaption>
</figure>
